WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.001
Just days

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.668
after the one

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.336
year anniversary of Russia's invasion

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.304
of Ukraine,

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:05.338
German Chancellor

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.172
Olaf Schulz

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.640
traveled to Washington to meet

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.075
with President Biden.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.610
The war and its ripple effects

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.244
were topics

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.146
one, two and three on the agenda

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:15.315
the White House publicly announced.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.750
Right after he left the White House.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:17.550
Chancellor Schulz

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.585
agreed to sit down

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:22.022
for an exclusive interview with me,

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:23.123
Chancellor Schulz.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.158
Pleasure to have you on, sir.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.027
Thank you for having me.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.496
So the leader of the German opposition

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.532
Friedrich Marx, says today,

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.935
why is all officials in Washington?

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.904
What is he doing there?

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.105
I thought I'd give you a chance

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.740
to respond to him.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.575
I already told Parliament

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.309
what I'm doing here.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.211
I'm talking to the president.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.547
And this is not the first talk.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:48.815
I was here one year ago

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.050
but we met quite often.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.618
And we have a lot of phone

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.952
calls, video conferences

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.287
where we speak together.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:57.490
So this is part of a permanent dialog of

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.227
of the two nations of the president

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:01.961
and me.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.096
And it's

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:05.465
also a sign of a very good friendship

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.268
and cooperation of the two countries.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.402
How does

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.571
Joe Biden strike you as a leader?

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.572
You've met many leaders

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.273
all over the world.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:16.042
What strikes you about Biden? He is

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.379
very

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.649
informed about international relations.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.485
I think he's one of the most skilled

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.419
presidents

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.353
knowing how

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.688
things are running in the world,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:29.622
which is important

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.223
and times

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.724
that are becoming more dangerous

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.360
and will see a lot of changes.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.697
And he is really a good man.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.999
Looking at the transatlantic partnership,

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.634
which is so important for Europe,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:43.536
but also for peace of the world

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.371
and for Natal.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.340
And I think there is

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.609
something which we have in common.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.444
Looking at the people

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.114
you in the United States, call them

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.148
the middle class.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.516
And I think it is important

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:57.550
that we don't forget

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.852
the both their perspectives

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.687
and their lives and their hopes.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.289
And so I like him.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.658
When you were talking to President Biden,

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:08.628
you must have confronted

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.897
the reality that the war in Ukraine

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:11.865
does appear

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.199
to have settled

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.901
into something of a stalemate.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.303
Neither side is making major advances.

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.538
The Russians have

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.707
seemed to have made some advances.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.076
Where does it go from here?

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.511
Looking at the situation,

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.614
which looks like what you explained to us

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:30.483
we have to understand

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.619
where we are coming from.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:35.021
So it was the idea of Russia

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:35.922
that the

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.223
world conquered the whole country

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.324
in a very short time.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.026
They did not succeed.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:43.263
They had to regroup the troops back

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:43.997
from Kiev

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.065
where they started their invasion.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:47.467
Now they are doing this

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.602
very ugly, aggressive war

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.504
in the east of Ukraine.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.107
And Russia never expected the

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.311
strength of Ukraine, of the people,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.612
the braveness, how

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.948
they defend their country.

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:04.350
And he never expected that they are

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.453
what he is not accepting

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:09.756
and nation and all together.

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.193
And on the other hand, he

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:16.095
misjudged the unity of

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.231
Europe, of the United States

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:20.266
and all the Friends of Ukraine

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.202
and the permanent supply of weapons

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.670
we give to the Ukraine.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:26.306
And so they were able to to defend

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.874
their country

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.509
and they will be able to do it

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.877
in the future.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.478
It is very difficult to judge

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.880
what will be the

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.715
next things to happen in Ukraine.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.116
But there is something

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.251
which is absolutely clear.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.687
We will continue to support Ukraine

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.056
with financial humanitarian

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.860
aid, but also with with weapons.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.130
But if this continues for years, Ukraine

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.732
as a country will be destroyed.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.501
Its economy is already down 40,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.470
50%, depending on

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.838
what estimate you look at.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.139
Is there a point

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:00.506
at which

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.342
you have to start negotiations

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:05.411
and is there a deal to be had where,

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.746
you know, Ukraine

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.514
gets some kind of security guarantees

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.849
from NATO's

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.518
perhaps EU membership and in return

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:14.287
it accepts the reality

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.322
that it is not getting Crimea back.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.090
It is perhaps

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.024
not getting some parts

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.226
of the Donbass back

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.329
There will be no decisions

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.631
without the Ukrainians.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:26.132
We will not take decisions

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.467
instead of them.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.468
We support them.

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:29.736
But what should they would?

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.371
Would you encourage them to take these?

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.339
So we told them that they

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:35.908
can go for

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.011
membership in the European Union,

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.581
and they are very there are working to to

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.683
to make progress

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:44.917
and all the criteria

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.520
that are important for this.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.689
I think they know that we will

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.556
that we are ready

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:51.524
to organize

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:52.292
a certain way

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.360
of security guarantee for the country

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:56.496
in times of peace to come.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:04:58.398
We are not there yet.

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.232
And

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.869
to my view,

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.138
it is necessary that Putin understands

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.572
that he will not succeed

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.607
with his invasion

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:10.209
and his imperialistic aggression.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.112
And that he has to withdraw troops.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.748
This is the basis for talks.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:16.449
And if you look

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.284
at the proposals of the Ukrainians,

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:20.620
you are it's easy to understand

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.455
they are ready for peace,

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:24.457
but there must be something done.

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.492
And this has to be done by Putin.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.195
Next on GPS,

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:29.796
more of

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.164
my exclusive interview

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.732
with the chancellor of Germany,

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.733
Olaf Schulz.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:36.169
No one really expected that one year ago

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.671
that we would easily

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.907
economically survive a situation

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:42.642
where there is no gas supply

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:43.576
to Germany

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.144
and many parts of Europe

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:46.713
from Russia anymore.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.781
Chancellor Schulz, let me ask you about

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:51.918
your extraordinary

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.720
speech to the German Bundestag,

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.987
where you talked about

00:05:54.987 --> 00:05:56.222
a kind of revolution,

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:58.591
a turning of German foreign policy.

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.961
The whole world looked at it

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.062
and was struck by

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.098
what an extraordinary statement it was.

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.800
But the action has not really followed.

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.203
You talked about $100 billion

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.437
that was going to be spent,

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.339
an increase in defense spending.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.974
I think something like 8 billion

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.310
is going to be spent this year.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.580
Is is there what is stopping

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.814
you from

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.517
making your actions match your words?

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:25.952
First,

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.020
I announced that we will supply

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.188
weapons to Ukraine

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.457
and give all the necessary financial aid.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.459
And we are now the strongest

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:34.627
supporter of Ukraine

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:35.795
in continental Europe.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:38.097
And we will continue to be it.

00:06:38.264 --> 00:06:41.033
It is €14 billion which we spent

00:06:41.167 --> 00:06:42.802
in the one or the other way

00:06:42.802 --> 00:06:44.971
to support Ukraine in the last year.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.273
And this is also due to weapons

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.442
where we are acting together

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.510
with the United States

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.378
and other friends and

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:55.081
delivering a lot of very successful

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:58.084
weapons for the defense of Ukraine.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.653
The last decision was about combat

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:02.522
tanks together with the United States,

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.790
but it was supposed to same

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:04.857
when we discussed

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.025
about multiple rocket

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.527
launchers, for instance,

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:08.694
and similar

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:11.597
weapons necessary for Ukraine.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.100
So we deliver it in this case.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.636
And the second is that we

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.673
made our

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.976
independent from the supply of gas, coal

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:25.578
and oil from Russia.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.113
No one really expected that.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:29.582
One year ago, that we would easily

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:32.785
economically survive a situation

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.520
where there is no gas supply

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:35.455
to Germany

00:07:35.455 --> 00:07:37.657
and many parts of Europe from Russia.

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:38.591
Anymore.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:42.195
But we did in increasing the capacity

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.465
of of LNG imports

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:47.633
from the western ports of Europe,

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.302
and also building new ports

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:51.337
in the northern shores of Germany,

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:54.006
using for a longer time as we plant

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.642
coal plants, also using using

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.779
nuclear plants which were running out,

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:01.948
but we increased the

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:03.416
possibility for them

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:05.451
to produce electricity.

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:06.752
And so we made it

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.955
and nothing of what some

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.291
people expect to happen.

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.827
There is no economic crisis in Germany.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:18.130
There is there is no

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:22.201
gas shortage or something like that.

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:24.036
And there

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:26.405
has also been more very on defense.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:29.041
Now, and there is also social stability.

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:32.378
Yes, we spent altogether 300 billion

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:34.547
to stabilize our economy

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:36.282
and save for the pockets

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:38.184
of the normal people

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.285
that they can survive

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:40.019
a situation

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:42.088
of increasing prices

00:08:42.088 --> 00:08:44.423
and increased prices for energy,

00:08:44.824 --> 00:08:45.758
which we are

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:48.427
seeing that they are going down again.

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:49.095
And also,

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:51.163
we started with

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:53.266
investing more in our defense.

00:08:53.266 --> 00:08:55.067
And it is absolutely clear

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:57.904
that we will go to 2% of our GDP, as is

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.273
agreed in later

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:03.009
when we are starting with this and

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.544
we are not spending a billion,

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.145
we are spending quite a lot

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.780
because we already have

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.649
the highest defense budget

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:10.683
in the European Union,

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:13.052
to be very clear as Germany.

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:15.621
But we are willing to increase this.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.757
But it is not that we are going to go

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:19.125
to a shopping

00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:20.293
mall and saying,

00:09:20.293 --> 00:09:22.094
I want to buy this or this,

00:09:22.094 --> 00:09:22.828
and it is

00:09:22.828 --> 00:09:23.729
even different

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.097
as if we would buy buy

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.999
some cars or trucks

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:29.101
which you can ask companies to do

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:30.903
and you will have them

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:33.205
right the next day or two or three

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:34.740
or six months time.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:36.342
In many cases, we have to

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.244
make the

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.278
industry starting

00:09:39.278 --> 00:09:40.046
their production

00:09:40.046 --> 00:09:42.315
and delivering this to us.

00:09:42.315 --> 00:09:44.183
And this is the idea behind

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:47.420
200 billion fund which was agreed

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.287
by the Parliament

00:09:48.287 --> 00:09:50.923
with a two thirds majority

00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:53.993
that we can take now the decisions

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.394
that are necessary

00:09:55.394 --> 00:09:59.465
for the long term supply of our army.

00:10:00.232 --> 00:10:02.268
And this will be about tanks

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:05.371
and it will be about our defense

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:07.273
and it will be about ammunition.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.240
And my idea is

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.775
that we have to change the way

00:10:09.775 --> 00:10:11.677
how we are dealing with the

00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:12.678
defense industry.

00:10:12.678 --> 00:10:14.013
So we need

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:15.748
and this is also a lesson we learned now

00:10:15.748 --> 00:10:17.850
from Ukraine and the war.

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.619
The Russians started against Ukraine.

00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.654
We need a permanent supply.

00:10:21.654 --> 00:10:22.922
So the main weapons

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:25.625
we use should be produced permanently.

00:10:25.992 --> 00:10:26.926
This is also

00:10:26.926 --> 00:10:29.028
for all the necessary maintenance,

00:10:29.028 --> 00:10:30.630
and this is also for ammunition.

